# Stack logs

When diagnosing dashboard hangs (“Waiting on Cube”), slow tiles, Cube errors, BI chart failures, or warehouse contention on uat111, **run the log CLI before hypothesising**.

```bash
python3 /root/DEV/data-cube/scripts/stack_logs.py snapshot
```

Then narrow:

| Symptom | Command |
|---|---|
| Cube Continue wait / SQL API | `… cube --since 30m --grep 'Continue wait'` |
| Chart / Celery error | `… bi --service worker --since 1h --grep Error` |
| FX / payments saturating RS | `… jobs --which all` then `… rs --minutes 60` |
| TLS / host routing | `… edge --tail 80` |

Full map: [docs/LOGS.md](docs/LOGS.md). Never print `.env` secrets. Prefer evidence from these logs over “probably”.
